#1 StructMark 2.0 Candidate Guide

The website keeps the existing 1.6 documentation and a separate 2.0 candidate engine. The Playground provides a syntax-version selector. In 2.0 mode it uses the shared Parser and HTML renderer from src/v2. This candidate does not yet implement every legacy 1.6 feature.

#2 Distinctive features

- Directive aliases and full names normalize to the same semantic AST.
- Native bracket-delimited tables with basic column types.
- A Schema subset for JSON objects with required and optional fields.
- Cross-file references validated by the workspace CLI.

#2 Example

```sm
#1 Data Report (#report)
&w[Warning]
This is a warning.
&e
&tbl
[Name:string][Count:number]
[A][12]
&e
See (#report).
```

#2 Command line

```bash
node bin/sm2.mjs check examples/v2-complete.sm
node bin/sm2.mjs html examples/v2-complete.sm
node bin/sm2.mjs workspace examples/workspace
```

#2 Release status

The version is 2.0.0-rc.1 (source candidate). Consult docs/STRUCTMARK_V2_RELEASE_EVIDENCE.md for executable validation results and docs/MD_SM_TOKEN_REPORT.md for the real-tokenizer `.md` versus `.sm` comparison. The measurements describe this corpus; they are not a guarantee that every document is shorter.
